{"pk": "1254", "sid": "PKDB00769", "name": "Dayyih2017", "licence": "open", "access": "public", "date": "2024-04-24", "group_count": 1, "individual_count": 0, "intervention_count": 2, "output_count": 132, "output_calculated_count": 24, "subset_count": 4, "timecourse_count": 4, "scatter_count": 0, "reference": {"pk": 1261, "study": {"sid": "PKDB00769", "name": "Dayyih2017"}, "pmid": "28894622", "sid": "28894622", "name": "Dayyih2017", "doi": "10.1155/2017/8489471", "title": "A Liquid Chromatography-Tandem Mass Spectrometry Method for Evaluation of Two Brands of Enalapril 20\u2009mg Tablets in Healthy Human Volunteers.", "abstract": "Enalapril is an angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor used for treatment of hypertension and chronic heart disease. Enalaprilat is its active metabolite responsible for the activity. This study aimed to develop and validate a method for enalapril and enalaprilat analysis and to determine the bioequivalence of two tablet formulae of enalapril. LC-MS/MS bioanalytical method was developed and validated and then applied to evaluate the bioavailability of two enalapril formulae. Antihyperglycemic sitagliptin was used as internal standard (IS). The method was accurate for the within- and between-days analysis, and precise CV% was <5%, being linear over the calibration range 1.0-200.0\u2009ng/ml. Stability was >85% and the LOD was 0.907 and 0.910\u2009ng/ml for enalapril and enalaprilat, respectively, and LLOQ was 1\u2009ng/ml. The pharmacokinetic parameters", "journal": "Journal of analytical methods in chemistry", "date": "2017-08-15", "authors": [{"pk": 7259, "first_name": "Wael Abu", "last_name": "Dayyih"}, {"pk": 7260, "first_name": "Mohammed", "last_name": "Hamad"}, {"pk": 7261, "first_name": "Ahmad Abu", "last_name": "Awwad"}, {"pk": 7262, "first_name": "Eyad", "last_name": "Mallah"}, {"pk": 7263, "first_name": "Zainab", "last_name": "Zakarya"}, {"pk": 7264, "first_name": "Alice Abu", "last_name": "Dayyih"}, {"pk": 7265, "first_name": "Tawfiq", "last_name": "Arafat"}]}, "reference_date": "2017-08-15", "creator": {"username": "shubhankarpalwankar", "first_name": "Shubhankar", "last_name": "Palwankar"}, "curators": [{"rating": 4.0, "username": "shubhankarpalwankar", "first_name": "Shubhankar", "last_name": "Palwankar"}, {"rating": 0.0, "username": "mkoenig", "first_name": "Matthias", "last_name": "K\u00f6nig"}], "collaborators": [], "comments": [], "descriptions": [{"pk": 4610, "text": "Thirty healthy adult male volunteers"}, {"pk": 4611, "text": "Volunteers were also informed not to take any medication and alcohol for at least 1 week before starting the study. In addition, they were fasted for 12hrs with free access to water"}, {"pk": 4612, "text": "enalapril (20mg tablet)"}, {"pk": 4613, "text": "After fasting period (12hrs, overnight), each volunteer was given an oral dose containing 20mg of enalapril either \u201cA, reference\u201d or \u201cB, tested\u201d formula with 200mL of water"}, {"pk": 4614, "text": "blood sampling at 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, 1.00, 1.33, 1.66, 2.00, 2.50, 3.00,3.50,4.00,4.50,5.00,6.00,8.00,10.00,12.00,24.00,48.0, and 72.00\u201dhours"}], "files": [{"pk": 15162, "name": "data/Dayyih2017_Fig5.png", "file": "/media/data/Dayyih2017_Fig5.png"}, {"pk": 15160, "name": "data/.Dayyih2017_Fig5.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Dayyih2017_Fig5.tsv"}, {"pk": 15165, "name": "data/Dayyih2017_Fig6.png", "file": "/media/data/Dayyih2017_Fig6.png"}, {"pk": 15163, "name": "data/.Dayyih2017_Fig6.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Dayyih2017_Fig6.tsv"}, {"pk": 15161, "name": "data/Dayyih2017.pdf", "file": "/media/data/Dayyih2017.pdf"}, {"pk": 15166, "name": "data/Dayyih2017_Tab6.png", "file": "/media/data/Dayyih2017_Tab6.png"}, {"pk": 15169, "name": "data/.Dayyih2017_Tab6.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Dayyih2017_Tab6.tsv"}, {"pk": 15164, "name": "data/.Dayyih2017_TabGroups.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.Dayyih2017_TabGroups.tsv"}, {"pk": 15167, "name": "data/.Dayyih2017_TabInterventions.tsv", "file": "/media/data/.D